.TH MW 1 "2026-09-06" "MemoryWhale 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw \- record whole terminal sessions into local MemoryWhale storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw
.RB [ --live ]
.RI [ --notes
.IR text ]
.br
.B mw list
.br
.B mw show
.I id
.br
.B mw search
.I text
.br
.B mw git-fix
.RI [ id ]
.br
.B mw github context
.I pull-request-number
.br
.B mw integrate
.RB { claude | rho }
.RB [ --revert ]
.br
.B mw integrate hermes
.br
.B mw integrate rho
.RB [ --http
.RI [ url ]]
.RB [ --token
.IR secret ]
.br
.B mw mark
.I text
.br
.B mw remember
.I text
.br
.B mw rm
.RB [ session | command ]
.I id
.br
.B mw prune
.RB [ --min-bytes
.IR n ]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.br
.B mw share
.RB [ session | command ]
.I id
.RB [ -o
.IR file ]
.br
.B mw discard
.br
.B mw replay
.I run-id
.br
.B mw export
.RI [ project:name ]
.br
.B mw import
.I bundle|sqlite
.br
.B mw push
.I ssh-host
.br
.B mw pull
.I ssh-host
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B mw context
.RI [ project:name ]
.RB [ --last-error ]
.RB [ --limit
.IR n ]
.br
.B mw agent
.RI [ session-id ]
.br
.B mw ask
.RI [ question ]
.RB [ --chat
.IR target ]
.RB [ --session ]
.RB [ --no-open ]
.br
.B mw doctor
.br
.B mw global
.RB { on | off | status }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw
starts your login shell inside a recorded subshell (via the system
.BR script (1)
tool) and captures every command and all output until you
.B exit
the subshell. The session is then stored in a local SQLite database; nothing
is ever uploaded.
.PP
The raw transcript is written under
.I <data_local>/MemoryWhale/sessions/
and the cleaned, searchable transcript plus metadata into
.IR <data_local>/MemoryWhale/memorywhale.sqlite3 .
On Linux
.I <data_local>
is
.IR ~/.local/share .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "mw [--notes " text ]
Record a session. Attach an optional note.
.TP
.B mw list
List recorded sessions (id, start time, size, note).
.TP
.BI "mw show " id
Print the full faithful transcript of session
.IR id .
.TP
.BI "mw search " text
Rank command runs, session transcripts, and notes by relevance. Results include
namespaced memory IDs, source types, and producing-agent labels.
Use
.B --explain
for ranking reasons. Inline filters include
.BR tag:X ,
.BR source:command|session|note|document|conversation ,
.BR agent:claude|rho|terminal ,
.BR before:YYYY-MM-DD ,
.BR after:YYYY-MM-DD ,
and
.BR limit:N .
Agent is separate from source type: a Claude shell capture is still a command.
.B terminal
matches NULL provenance (terminal/manual or legacy records), not a stored
agent string or proof of human authorship.
.TP
.BI "mw explain " "id [query]"
Show the per-signal score breakdown for one namespaced memory ID from search.
.TP
.BI "mw git-fix " [id]
Diagnose the last failed
.B git
command (or a specific
.I command_run
.IR id ):
recognizes common failure shapes (push rejected, merge conflict, dirty working
tree, diverged branches, unrelated histories, SSH auth), explains what
happened, prints the fix, and checks whether this has come up before or was
already resolved via
.BR "mw remember" .
.TP
.BI "mw github context " pull-request-number
Explicitly fetch bounded, redacted PR metadata, CI check-runs, classic commit
statuses, and reviews
through the existing
.BR gh (1)
login, using the repository containing the current working directory.
Prints context without checking out code, submitting a review, automatically
saving to memory, or background synchronization. An independently enabled
terminal recorder can still capture the printed output.
.TP
.B mw integrate claude [--revert]
Install Claude Code MCP registration, capture hook, and bundled memory-use
skill. The hook uses
.BR "mw-remember --from-hook claude" ;
no checkout or Python runtime is required.
.B claude-code
is an alias. Revert removes the integration without deleting memory.
.TP
.BI "mw integrate rho [--revert] [--http [" url "]] [--token " secret ]
Install Rho MCP registration, capture hook, and skill. Stdio is the default;
.B --http
selects the
.B POST /mcp
endpoint (default http://127.0.0.1:7071/mcp).
.B --token
requires
.BR --http .
LAN HTTP requires a token; the installer prints the authorization environment
setup for the client. Revert removes the integration without deleting memory.
Hooks capture supported events; a skill guides memory use, not automatic
task-start recall, failure lookup, or pre-compaction saving.
.TP
.B mw integrate hermes
Register the MCP server in Hermes Agent's config.
.TP
.BI "mw mark " text
Bookmark the current debugging moment with a note.
.TP
.BI "mw remember " text
Save a freeform lesson or conclusion (e.g. what actually fixed a bug), so
.BR "mw search" " and " "mw context"
surface it later instead of it being re-derived. Shares storage with
.BR "mw mark" .
.TP
.BI "mw memory stale " id
Retire an outdated lesson while preserving its row.
.TP
.BI "mw memory supersede " "old-id new-id"
Replace a lesson with a newer memory without deleting the original evidence.
.TP
.B mw memory compact [--apply]
Preview conservative evidence compaction; only
.B --apply
changes retained text. Preserves rows and original session files.
Threshold options are
.BR --min-session-bytes ,
.BR --stale-days ,
and
.BR --max-output-bytes ,
each followed by a number.
.TP
.BI "mw link " "a b [rel:type]"
Link two namespaced memory IDs; the default relation is related.
.TP
.BI "mw unlink " "a b [rel:type]"
Remove a typed link between two memories.
.TP
.BI "mw links " id
Show a memory's linked neighbors in both directions.
.TP
.BI "mw rm [session|command] " id
Delete a saved session (default) or command run by id. A session's transcript
file is removed too, so the dashboard cannot re-recover it.
.TP
.BI "mw prune [--min-bytes " n "] [--dry-run]"
Delete empty/near-empty auto-recorded sessions \(em the noise left by opening a
terminal and closing it. Only removes
.B interrupted
sessions below the byte threshold (default 200); deliberate finished sessions
are kept.
.B --dry-run
shows what would go without deleting.
.TP
.BI "mw share [session|command] " id " [-o " file ]
Write a self-contained, redacted HTML page for one memory (reusing
.BR mw-view (1))
so you can send it to a teammate. Defaults to
.IR memory-<id>.html .
.TP
.B mw discard
Run inside a recorded shell to throw the current session away: it is not saved
when you exit. Useful when a terminal turned out to be garbage.
.TP
.BI "mw replay " run-id
Rerun a saved command run from the database.
.TP
.B mw demo
Seed a small demo terminal-memory dataset (for trying the dashboard and search
without recording anything first).
.TP
.BI "mw export " [project:name]
Export memory to a bundle (Markdown, JSON, and a SQLite copy), optionally
scoped to a project tag.
.TP
.BI "mw import " bundle|sqlite
Merge another machine's exported memory into this one, skipping duplicates.
.TP
.BI "mw push " ssh-host
Snapshot this machine's memory, copy it to
.I ssh-host
with
.BR scp (1),
and run
.B mw import
there. Requires
.B mw
installed on the remote.
.TP
.BI "mw pull " ssh-host " [" path ]
Copy another machine's memory database here with
.BR scp (1)
and merge it in. The mirror of
.BR "mw push" .
Defaults to the remote's Linux data directory; pass
.I path
to point at a different location.
.TP
.BI "mw context " [project:name] " [--last-error] [--limit " n ]
Print a compact, token-budgeted digest of recent failed commands and sessions,
suitable for pasting into an AI agent.
.TP
.BI "mw agent " [session-id]
Export a full session transcript (plus recent failures) as Markdown on stdout,
to hand to an AI agent later. Defaults to the most recent session. Redirect or
pipe it, e.g.\& \fBmw agent > session.md\fR or \fBmw agent | pbcopy\fR.
.TP
.BI "mw ask " "[question] " "[--chat target] [--session] [--no-open]"
Package the most recent failure \(em exact error, similar past failures,
saved lessons \(em into one debugging prompt, copy it to the clipboard, and
open your chat. Paste into whatever chat you already pay for; no API key, no
per-token billing \(em it rides your flat-rate chat subscription instead of
metered API calls.
.BI --chat " target"
picks the chat:
.BR chatgpt " (default), " claude ", " gemini ,
or any http(s) URL; set
.B MEMORYWHALE_CHAT
to change the default.
.B --session
appends the tail of the current session;
.B --no-open
skips launching the browser. Prints the payload instead if no clipboard tool
(pbcopy/xclip/wl-copy) is available.
.TP
.B mw doctor
Check the install: data directory, database, the
.BR script (1)
dependency, auto-record hook status, the local MCP server, and Claude Code
and Rho integration (MCP registration, capture hook, and skill).
Each integration component is checked independently; missing optional clients
are not detected, not failed installs. The bounded MCP probe discovers or
initializes the protocol and lists tools, without calling memory tools,
running client CLIs, changing configuration, or printing tokens.
.TP
.B mw tui
Browse memory interactively, including pending agent-authored lessons
for review.
.TP
.B mw pet [--watch]
Show the whale whose mood reflects the store; optionally animate it. Read-only.
.TP
.B mw audit
Inspect capture policy, retained volume, and high-volume sources.
.TP
.B mw status
Print the effective capture mode for this directory and why it applies.
.TP
.B mw hooks install|uninstall [pwsh]
Install or remove lightweight per-command shell capture, without output.
.TP
.BI "mw sync-mempalace " "[--wing name] [--limit n] [--dry-run]"
Explicitly mirror memories into a configured MemPalace server, idempotently by
memory ID. Dry-run prints the plan without contacting the server.
.TP
.B mw --version
Print the product version without opening the database; alias
.BR -V .
.TP
.B mw global on
Wire a shell-startup hook so every new interactive terminal auto-records.
.TP
.B mw global off
Stop auto-recording new terminals (open recordings continue until you exit).
.TP
.B mw global status
Show whether auto-recording is enabled and where it is wired.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR
Override the data directory (default
.IR <data_local>/MemoryWhale ).
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Override the Claude Code configuration directory used by integration and doctor.
.TP
.B RHO_HOME
Override the Rho configuration directory used by integration and doctor.
.TP
.B MW_RECORDING
Set to 1 inside a recorded shell; the global hook checks it to avoid nested
recordings.
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_NO_REDACT
Set to disable secret redaction of captured output (stored raw). By default,
common secret shapes (API keys, tokens, passwords, PEM blocks) are scrubbed
before storage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/MemoryWhale/memorywhale.sqlite3
Session and command database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/MemoryWhale/sessions/
Raw session transcripts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw-run (1),
.BR mw-remember (1),
.BR mw-serve (1),
.BR mw-mcp (1),
.BR mw-view (1),
.BR mw-recover (1),
.BR script (1)
